## 🏛️ PILLAR 1: THE WORKFORCE & COGNITIVE FRICTION  
*(Preserving the "Bottom Rungs" of Human Development)*

**The Challenge**: Premature automation of entry-level tasks deprives young professionals of the cognitive friction required to build foundational judgment.

**The ZEM Solution: Cognitive Friction Protocol (都攝六根 at Work)**
- **Policy 1.1**: Mandate that junior staff produce "first drafts" unassisted in government and regulated industries. AI may verify and edit, but humans must sign the final output (Condition C1: Named Human Signature).
- **Policy 1.2**: Phase AI adoption over a 10-year horizon, ensuring *time to retrain* exceeds *rate of automation* ($R \\\\ge 1$). Retrenchment remains a last resort; the metric is successful human upskilling.

**AIE Effect**: By restricting the "motion" of premature delegation, we force the energy of human development to emit as mature, resilient professional judgment.

